From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xob0t <32616886+xob0t@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:06:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] Floating-point negation through a mask held in a
 register

"xorps x, m" with the sign mask of a double is lifted lane by lane. Where the mask was
loaded once, ahead of a loop, its lanes reach the XOR through merges and are constants
only after normalization: the double came out as "high half ^ 80000000h" beside
"low half ^ 0", never folded back into "-x". Such a value passed in a stack slot was then
read as its low half alone (an int where a double belongs, with no marker), and one passed
in a register as the bits of a double.

- Normalizer.RefoldTruncations: a Concat of a top half under a bitwise mask and a bottom
  half that is not (or is under the op's identity) is the whole under the 64-bit mask,
  where the halves are those of a double (cut out of a double's bits, the top lane of a
  call's vector result, or merges of such): a Vector2 with its y negated looks the same
  and is left alone. The whole folds or its merges rejoin as before
  (REWIND_NO_MASKED_HALVES).
- IrBuilder.IsLowHalf: the bottom half of "x ^ m" (or "|", or "&") is the bottom half of x
  when m leaves the bottom half alone (REWIND_NO_BOTTOM_MASKS).
- HirBuilder.FloatAt: a double in a stack slot made of two 32-bit values is both halves,
  not the low one (REWIND_NO_DOUBLE_HALVES).
- HirBuilder.SignedLanes: a double argument or return in the two lanes of a register,
  the top one under the sign or magnitude mask, is "-x" or "Math.Abs(x)"
  (REWIND_NO_SIGNED_LANES).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
